## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of 128-bit arithmetic using hi/lo, avoiding loops, and applying a scalable, branchless popcount.

## Key Concepts
- 128-bit representation via hi/lo
- SWAR/parallel bit counting
- Endianness and safe casting between types

## Code Example
```c
static inline uint64_t popcount64(uint64_t x){
  x -= (x >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL;
  x = (x & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((x >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  return (x * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;
}

uint8_t popcount128(uint128 x){
  return (uint8_t)(popcount64(x.hi) + popcount64(x.lo));
}
``` 

