- How would you adapt this to accumulate using wider accumulators? 
- What is the performance impact on platforms with native popcount intrinsics?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to perform parallel, lane-specific bit manipulation on a 128-bit value without branching.

## Key Concepts
- Video: decompose 128-bit into four 32-bit words; W0 is lo, W3 is hi
- Per-lane rotation: Ri = (Wi << mi) | (Wi >> ((32 - mi) & 31)); mi = ni & 31
- Reassemble lanes in the same order; handle edge cases with safe shifts

## Code Example
```javascript
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;
uint128 rotateWords128(uint128 x, unsigned n0, unsigned n1, unsigned n2, unsigned n3) {
  unsigned m0 = n0 & 31, m1 = n1 & 31, m2 = n2 & 31, m3 = n3 & 31;
  uint32_t w0 = (uint32_t)(x.lo);
  uint32_t w1 = (uint32_t)(x.lo >> 32);
  uint32_t w2 = (uint32_t)(x.hi);
  uint32_t w3 = (uint32_t)(x.hi >> 32);
  uint32_t r0 = (w0 << m0) | (w0 >> ((32 - m0) & 31));
  uint32_t r1 = (w1 << m1) | (w1 >> ((32 - m1) & 31));
  uint32_t r2 = (w2 << m2) | (w2 >> ((32 - m2) & 31));
  uint32_t r3 = (w3 << m3) | (w3 >> ((32 - m3) & 31));
  uint128 z;
  z.lo = ((uint64_t)r1 << 32) | r0;
  z.hi = ((uint64_t)r3 << 32) | r2;
  return z;
}
```

